AI-Powered Alcohol Label Verification Prototype
Prepared For: TTB Compliance Division Prototype Evaluation
 Prepared By: Amelia Dahn
 Project Type: Standalone Proof-of-Concept (POC)
 Version: 2.0
 Date: May 2026

1. Executive Summary
This project proposes a standalone AI-powered alcohol label verification application designed to assist TTB compliance agents in reviewing beverage labels against submitted application data.
The prototype focuses on reducing repetitive manual verification work by automatically extracting information from alcohol label images and comparing it against structured application data. The system is intended to improve reviewer efficiency while maintaining human oversight for nuanced compliance decisions.
The application is intentionally designed as a proof-of-concept and will not directly integrate with COLAs Online or internal TTB systems during this phase.
The prototype demonstrates how OCR, AI-assisted parsing, and automated rule validation can modernize portions of the label review process while remaining practical for real-world government workflows.

2. Problem Statement
TTB compliance agents currently perform a largely manual review process for alcohol beverage labels. Reviewers visually inspect label artwork and compare required regulatory information against application forms.
This workflow creates several operational challenges:
High reviewer workload
Repetitive manual verification tasks
Processing bottlenecks during peak seasons
Inconsistent review speed
Limited scalability
Reviewer fatigue
Stakeholder interviews revealed that many reviews involve repetitive field matching rather than complex legal interpretation. Agents frequently spend time verifying:
Brand names
Alcohol content
Net contents
Government warnings
Beverage classifications
Bottler/importer information
Previous modernization pilots failed largely due to poor performance and slow processing speeds. Reviewers indicated that any solution exceeding approximately five seconds per label would likely not be adopted.

3. Product Vision
Develop a lightweight, intuitive, AI-assisted review platform that:
Processes labels rapidly
Extracts mandatory label information automatically
Validates compliance against TTB requirements
Flags mismatches and formatting issues
Supports human review workflows
Handles both single and batch submissions
Works reliably with imperfect label images
The system should function as an intelligent assistant rather than a fully autonomous reviewer.

